course: dictionary
lesson: 14585
title: Compound words: playroom
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A compound word is two smaller words joined together to make one new word. Playroom is made from play and room.
explain: «The children ran into the playroom to find their toys.» Play is what you do for fun, and room is a space inside a building, so a playroom is a room for playing.
explain: You can often work out a compound word by joining the meanings of its two parts. Then check your meaning in the sentence. «Mum tidied the playroom after tea.» makes sense if a playroom is a room where toys are kept.
fact: A playroom is a room in a house, school or other building where children play and keep toys.
fact: «Playroom» is a compound word: «play» + «room».
fact: «The nursery has a playroom full of bricks and dolls.»
fact: Playrooms can be found in homes, nurseries, hospitals and waiting rooms.
fact: In stories, a playroom is a place of games and imagination.
exercise: «The children ran into the playroom to find their toys.» What is a playroom? | A kitchen for cooking dinner | A garden shed for tools | *A room where children play and keep toys
exercise: Which two smaller words are joined to make playroom? | play and rum | plan and room | *play and room
exercise: «Mum tidied the playroom after tea.» Where did Mum tidy? | Outside the school gate | In the garden under a tree | In the bath | *In the room where the toys are kept
test: «The hospital playroom had bright paints and a rocking horse.» Where would you find bright paints and a rocking horse? | At a bus stop | Under the sea | In a bank, behind the counter | *In a room for children to play in
test: What does the word play tell you about a playroom? | It is a room for washing | It is a room for sleeping | It is a room for cooking | *It is a room for playing
exam: Which of these is a playroom? | A classroom with desks and a board | *A room in a home where children play and keep their toys | A bedroom with a bed for sleeping | A bathroom with a bath and a sink
